; 1 - Branch distance forward
; A branch (BRA, BEQ, BNE, BSR ...) reaches -128 ... +127 bytes,
; counted from the address of the NEXT instruction.
;
; Try it:
;   - Hover over Edge and Over (lines 19 and 22): addresses $81 and $84.
;   - Delete the NOP in line 21: Over moves to $83, the error in
;     line 16 disappears (now exactly +127).
;   - Insert a line "NOP" right after line 17: Edge moves to $82,
;     now line 15 is too far (+128).
;   - While you type a new line, messages may move around briefly
;     until the line is complete.

            ORG     $00
            BRA     Edge            ; OK: at $00, next $02, target $81 = +127
            BRA     Over            ; ERROR: at $02, next $04, target $84 = +128
            BNE     Edge            ; OK: at $04, next $06, +123
            RMB     123             ; OK: space $06..$80
Edge        NOP                     ; OK: address $81
            RMB     1               ; OK: $82
            NOP                     ; OK: $83
Over        NOP                     ; OK: address $84
